        "547": {"synopsis":"DOS_OPEN's work: opens file number B on drive A, if it is free (bit 7 set in its file table\nbyte at $2320 + B).\n1. B of 16 or more, or the number in use: rc_number ($1D).\n2. DRIVE_CHECK for the drive; when it gives NZ, E must be below 3 and D 0, else rc_badname\n   ($14).\n3. $1C7B in the drive's bank (CALL_2006_BANK_W). Carry clear: step 4. Carry set: NZ gives\n   rc_badname; E = 0 rc_exists ($18); E = 1 or 2 opens with D = E - 1 and bit 1 set (step\n   5); E = 3 or 4 calls DRIVE_3E1F for the drive, then step 4; E 5 or more rc_badparam\n   ($15).\n4. D must be 1 or 2 (0 gives rc_nofile ($17), 3 or more rc_badparam), and is made 0 or 1.\n5. OPEN_VEC ($175C) for the drive with D; on success the file's table byte = the drive's\n   ($2006), and Z = bit 1 of D clear.\nEntry: A = the drive, B = the file number, D = the create action, E = the open action (the\naction numbers as DOS_OPEN's).\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear, A = the code.","comment":"IYh = the drive"},
        "549": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "550": {"comment":"File number 16 or more?"},
        "553": {"comment":"Yes: rc_number"},
        "555": {"comment":"The file table"},
