        "954": {"comment":"Free: carry set"},
        "956": {"comment":"Next number"},
        "958": {"comment":"Up to 15?"},
        "962": {"comment":"None: rc_number"},
        "964": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "966": {"synopsis":"RST $18's work: the word after the RST (high byte first) is stored at $3C53 for the code at\n$3C4D in DivMMC RAM, which is then called:\n1. The return address moved past the word; AF and DE kept.\n2. Port $E3 is read; GO_3CFD_BANK0 is called (port $E3 = $80, $3CFD); the old port value is\n   kept at $2002 and the word at $3C53.\n3. SP kept at $2016; $3C4D called with the caller's registers.\n4. Port $E3 back from $2002, by way of $1FF3 when it was $82 (the fetch at $1FF8 there ends\n   the automap).\nExit: AF, BC, DE, HL as the routine at $3C4D leaves them.","comment":"HL = the word's address"},
        "967": {"comment":"AF, DE kept"},
        "969": {"comment":"DE = the word, high byte first"},
        "972": {"comment":"Past it: the return address"},
        "973": {"comment":"Port $E3 as it was"},
        "975": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "976": {"comment":"Bank 0 code at $3CFD"},
        "979": {"comment":"A = the old port value"},
        "980": {"comment":"Kept at $2002"},
        "983": {"comment":"The word for $3C4D"},
        "987": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "988": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "989": {"comment":"HL back, return address set"},
        "990": {"comment":"SP kept at $2016"},
        "994": {"comment":"The routine at $3C4D"},
        "997": {"comment":"Its AF kept"},
        "998": {"comment":"The old port value"},
        "1001": {"comment":"Was it $82?"},
        "1003": {"comment":"Yes: the automap ended"},
        "1006": {"comment":"Port $E3 back"},
        "1008": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "1010": {"synopsis":"Calls IDE_BANK ($01BD) in NextZXOS ROM 2 with HL as given (kept at $2010 for CALL_ROM2). Not\ncalled from this ROM.","comment":"HL kept at $2010"},
        "1013": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_BANK"},
        "1016": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at HL in NextZXOS ROM 2:\n1. $3CFC pushed as the way back (ROM 2's DIVMMC_ENTER, which maps the DivMMC memory in\n   again), then HL.\n2. HL = the word at $2010; NextReg $8E = 2 (ROM 2).\n3. The RET at $1FF9 (the fetch there ends the automap) goes to the routine.\nJumped to from CALL_IDE_BANK and CARD_CAPACITY's $0EE3 (HL = $17DE, ROM 2's SD card size\nroutine).","comment":"Way back: ROM 2's $3CFC"},
        "1020": {"comment":"The routine"},
        "1021": {"comment":"HL from $2010"},
        "1024": {"comment":"ROM 2"},
        "1028": {"comment":"Go, automap off"},
        "1031": {"synopsis":"CALL $0407 + a word: calls that address in the DivMMC RAM bank in the byte at $2006\n(CALL_BANK_A_W), the routine getting the caller's AF.\nChanges: IY (= the caller's AF).","comment":"IY = AF"},
        "1034": {"comment":"A = the byte at $2006"},
        "1037": {"synopsis":"CALL $040D + a word: $2006 = A, then the word's address is called with port $E3 = bank A\n(bits 3-0; bits 7-6 as they are) and AF = IY (CALL_IN_BANK's way); bit 7 of A set drops the\ncall and fails with rc_nodrive ($16) (CALL_BANK_FAIL). Called from DRIVE_CALL_1BA8 and\n$1DAD, whose IYh is the drive.","comment":"Kept at $2006"},
        "1040": {"comment":"Bank bits and bit 7"},
        "1042": {"comment":"Bit 7: fail"},
        "1045": {"comment":"Alternate set"},
        "1046": {"comment":"HL' = the word's address"},
        "1047": {"comment":"DE', BC' kept"},
        "1049": {"comment":"B' = the bank"},
        "1050": {"comment":"AF = IY"},
        "1053": {"comment":"On with the word"},
        "1055": {"synopsis":"CALL $041F + a byte + a word: calls the word's address with port $E3 = the byte (the bank,\nbits 3-0) and bits 7-6 as they are, then port $E3 back. The routine gets the caller's AF,\nBC, DE, HL and returns its own; the alternate registers are kept. Called from CALL_204F_B1,\nthe five bank-12 routines at $0310-$032C, and $1E36.","comment":"Alternate set"},
        "1056": {"comment":"HL' = the bytes' address"},
        "1057": {"comment":"DE', BC' kept"},
        "1059": {"comment":"B' = the bank"},
        "1061": {"comment":"AF kept","synopsis":"CALL_IN_BANK's call: port $E3 = bank B', the word called, port $E3 and the alternate\nregisters back."},
        "1062": {"comment":"C' = port $E3 as it was"},
        "1065": {"comment":"CONMEM, MAPRAM kept"},
