        "1094": {"comment":"Main set"},
        "1095": {"comment":"Go"},
        "1096": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC side of NextZXOS ROM 2's RST $08 (its RST08_DIVMMC pushes $0448 before the DivMMC\nmemory is mapped in at $3D00), with A = the byte after that RST and HL = its word:\n1. Port $E3 = A; CALL_SAVED_HL calls HL with the caller's AF and HL.\n2. Port $E3 = 0; NextReg $8E = 2 (ROM 2); the RET at $1FF9 (the fetch there ends the\n   automap) goes to ROM 2's DIVMMC_BACK ($3F40).\nExit: AF as the routine left it.","comment":"Port $E3 = A"},
        "1098": {"comment":"The routine"},
        "1101": {"comment":"Its AF kept"},
        "1102": {"comment":"DivMMC memory paged out"},
        "1105": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "1106": {"comment":"ROM 2"},
        "1110": {"comment":"Back to ROM 2's $3F40"},
        "1114": {"comment":"Return, automap off"},
        "1117": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL with AF = the word at $5B56 and HL = the word at $5B52 (as NextZXOS ROM 2's RST\n$08 kept them).","comment":"Address to go to"},
        "1118": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "1123": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "1240": {"comment":"On in DivMMC RAM"},
        "1243": {"synopsis":"Not reached from this ROM: (HL) = 0, then BANK_LDIR (with DE = HL + 1, BC + 1 bytes\ncleared).","comment":"A = 0"},
        "1244": {"comment":"At HL"},
        "1245": {"synopsis":"LDIR with carry set: the copy NextZXOS ROM 2's RST $08 calls with port $E3 = $0C or $0D\n(DOS_RST08_BACK), with its caller's BC, DE and HL.","comment":"The copy"},
        "1247": {"comment":"Success"},
        "1249": {"synopsis":"CALL $04E1 + a byte: as RST $28 for IX: BC and DE = the 32-bit field at IX + the byte. HL\nkept.","comment":"HL = the byte's address"},
        "1250": {"comment":"C = the offset"},
