        "1988": {"synopsis":"Finds the buffer for sector BCDE of volume IX:\n1. The two records at $2332 (7 bytes each: flags, bit 0 in use, bit 1 changed, bit 2 a FAT\n   sector; the volume's IX; the sector, low byte first) are compared; a match is moved to\n   the front (BUF_TO_FRONT), carry set.\n2. Otherwise the least recently used buffer (the last of the order list, $2331) is written\n   out if changed (BUF_FLUSH), given the sector and IX with the flags = 1, and moved to the\n   front; carry clear (its contents still to be read).\nExit: HL = the buffer, IY = its record; carry set when the sector was there.","comment":"The first record"},
