        "2653": {"synopsis":"Finds FAT partition C (0 the first) on device A for the volume block at IX. Called from\n$0D09 and $0DED.\n1. BC + 1 must leave B = 0, else rc_invpartition ($38); B = C = the count.\n2. The device block copied to IX (DEVICE_COPY); a buffer tied to no volume (BUF_ASSIGN with\n   IX = 0) is kept at $202C for sector 0.\n3. For partition table slots 1-4 (IX+$2A): sector 0 read ($1EA5); without $55, $AA at its\n   end, rc_invpartition. A slot ($1BE + 16 x (n - 1)) of type nonzero gives IX+1 = its first\n   sector (+8) and IX+7 = its size (+$0C), and FAT_BPB_READ ($0B14) tries it; each one that\n   works counts B down.\n4. B at 0: the label. When the byte at IY (as FAT_BPB_READ left it) is $29, 11 bytes from 5\n   on are copied to $202E and DE = $202E; otherwise DE = $0EE9 (NO_NAME_TEXT). $1200 is\n   called; on carry with Z, HL = DE. Carry set.\n5. After slot 4: only partition 0 may be the whole device (IX+$2A = 0, tried by\n   FAT_BPB_READ, then step 4); otherwise rc_invpartition.\nExit: carry set on success; carry clear, A = the code.","comment":"Count + 1"},
        "2654": {"comment":"256 or more?"},
        "2656": {"comment":"Yes: fail"},
        "2659": {"comment":"B = C = the count"},
        "2660": {"comment":"Kept"},
