        "2858": {"synopsis":"No usable FAT volume: A = $38 (rc_invpartition in the API document's +3DOS list), carry\nclear.","comment":"rc_invpartition"},
        "2860": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "2862": {"synopsis":"Reads sector 0 of the volume at IX (the boot sector) into the buffer at ($202C) and fills\nthe\ndescriptor from its parameter block.\n1. Bytes per sector (+$0B) must be 512; sectors per cluster (+$0D) not 0, kept at IX+$21.\n2. Reserved sectors (+$0E), not 0, at IX+$19 (the first FAT's sector).\n3. A 16-bit FAT size (+$16) marks FAT16: IX+$13 = $80; 0 there means FAT32 (IX+$13 = 0) and\nthe 32-bit size (+$24). The size goes to IX+$14, the number of FATs (+$10, not 0) to IX+$18.\n4. Reserved + FATs x size is the root directory's sector on FAT16 (IX+$1D, and its sector\ncount from the root entries (+$11, a multiple of 16) at IX+$1B); FAT32 needs 0 root\nentries and keeps the root cluster (+$2C) at IX+$1D.\n5. The data area's sector minus two clusters goes to IX+$26 (the sector of cluster 0).\n6. The data sectors (total (+$13 or +$20) minus the data start) over sectors per cluster,\nplus 1, is the highest cluster number, at IX+$22; 4084 clusters or fewer (FAT12) fail.\nHalf of it is the first free-cluster hint (IX+$2F).\n7. FAT32: the FSInfo sector (+$30, kept at IX+$33) with its signature 'rrAa' at $1E4 gives\nthe free count (IX+$2B) and the next-free hint (IX+$2F), bit 6 of IX+$13 set; without\nit the hint's value stands for the free count. FAT16: free count $FFFF0000 (not known).\nEntry: IX = the volume's descriptor (its first sector at IX+1).\nExit: carry set, IY = the boot sector's extended-signature byte (+$26 FAT16, +$42 FAT32);\nor carry clear and A = $38.","comment":"BCDE = 0: the volume's sector 0"},
