        "3344": {"synopsis":"BCDE = the free cluster count of the volume at IX (IX+$2B; $FFFF0000 when not known, as\n$09CC tests), carry set.","comment":"BCDE = the free count"},
        "3348": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3350": {"synopsis":"Read error: the stacked words dropped, carry clear.","comment":"Clean the stack"},
        "3354": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITON_READ (the vector at $010C; so spelt in the API document): builds a 64-byte\npartition entry for partition BC of unit A at HL, the partition mounted on the scratch\ndescriptor at $203E by $0A5D.\n1. Byte 0: '0' + its slot in the partition table (0 with none), byte 1 '>'.\n2. Bytes 2-12: the volume label returned by $0A5D, then three spaces.\n3. Byte 16: the type, $10 for FAT16, $11 for FAT32; then six $FF bytes.\n4. Bytes 23-26: the size from IX+7; the 37 bytes to the end 0.\nEntry: A = the unit, BC = the partition (0 the first), HL = the buffer.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error. BC and IX kept.","comment":"Kept"},
        "3358": {"comment":"The scratch descriptor"},
        "3362": {"comment":"Mount the partition"},
        "3366": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "3368": {"comment":"Its slot in the table"},
        "3371": {"comment":"As a digit"},
        "3375": {"comment":"Then '>'"},
        "3378": {"comment":"The label's 11 bytes"},
        "3385": {"comment":"Three spaces"},
        "3387": {"synopsis":"One space."},
        "3392": {"comment":"The type: $10"},
        "3394": {"comment":"FAT16?"},
        "3400": {"comment":"FAT32: $11"},
        "3401": {"synopsis":"Six $FF bytes after the type."},
        "3402": {"comment":"Six $FF bytes"},
        "3404": {"synopsis":"One $FF."},
        "3409": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "3410": {"comment":"HL = IX+7, the size"},
        "3417": {"comment":"Four bytes"},
        "3421": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "3422": {"comment":"37 zeros (C is 0)"},
        "3424": {"synopsis":"One 0."},
        "3428": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3429": {"synopsis":"BC and IX restored.","comment":"Restored"},
        "3433": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_FIND (the vector at $0109): finds the partition of unit A named at HL by\nbuilding each partition's entry at $2200 (PART_ENTRY_READ) in turn.\n1. A name with '>' as its second byte is matched on all 16 bytes ('p>' and the label);\nwhen only its label part is blank, 'p>' alone decides.\n2. Otherwise the 14 bytes of the label part are matched; an all-blank name matches the\nfirst partition.\nEntry: A = the unit, HL = the name.\nExit: carry set and BC = the partition number (its volume mounted on $203E); or carry\nclear and A = the error of the first partition not there ($38).","comment":"The first partition"},
        "3436": {"synopsis":"One partition's entry built and compared.","comment":"Unit, number, name stacked"},
        "3439": {"comment":"Its entry built here"},
        "3445": {"comment":"The name"},
        "3446": {"comment":"No more partitions"},
        "3449": {"comment":"The name's second byte"},
        "3451": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "3455": {"comment":"Compare 16 bytes"},
        "3458": {"comment":"From the entry's start"},
        "3461": {"comment":"Carry: the full form"},
        "3464": {"comment":"Otherwise 14 bytes"},
        "3466": {"comment":"From the label"},
        "3468": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "3469": {"synopsis":"One byte compared.","comment":"A byte of the entry"},
        "3471": {"comment":"Same as the name's?"},
        "3475": {"comment":"More to compare?"},
        "3478": {"synopsis":"A match: BC = the partition number, carry set.","comment":"Found: BC = the number"},
        "3481": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3483": {"synopsis":"A difference: in the full form at the label's first byte, a blank label still matches.","comment":"Label form: no match"},
        "3485": {"comment":"The label's first byte?"},
        "3490": {"comment":"Is the name's label all spaces?"},
        "3495": {"synopsis":"One byte of the label: a space?"},
        "3501": {"comment":"Yes: a match"},
        "3503": {"synopsis":"The next partition.","comment":"Next partition"},
        "3509": {"synopsis":"No partition left: carry clear, A = the mount error.","comment":"Drop number and unit"},
        "3512": {"synopsis":"The partition is mounted already: A = $3B (rc_partopen), three words dropped."},
        "3513": {"synopsis":"Two words dropped; IX restored, carry as it is."},
        "3518": {"synopsis":"Maps drive E to partition BC of unit D (the vector at $010F, reached from the jump at\n$0169 by IDE_DOS_MAP's call in ROM 2).\n1. Every mapped drive (the 16-word table at $2E6E, DIR_REC pointers) is checked: one on the\nsame partition (IX+$11) of the same unit (bit 0 of IX+$10) gives error $3B.\n2. The drive's descriptor ($2A10 + 53 x E) is mounted by $0A5D.\n3. Its directory record ($2D60 + 15 x E) is set to the root (DIR_REC_ROOT) and its address\nstored in the drive's word of $2E6E.\nEntry: E = the drive 0-15, D = the unit, BC = the partition.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error. IX kept.","comment":"Kept"},
        "3520": {"comment":"A = the drive, E = drive + 1"},
        "3523": {"comment":"HL = its word in the drive table"},
        "3527": {"comment":"Stacked, then unit and drive"},
        "3529": {"comment":"Drive 0"},
        "3530": {"synopsis":"One drive of the table checked.","comment":"Drive number stacked"},
        "3531": {"comment":"Is it mapped?"},
        "3536": {"comment":"HL = its directory record"},
        "3537": {"comment":"DE = the record's descriptor"},
        "3540": {"comment":"IY = it"},
        "3543": {"comment":"Same partition?"},
        "3555": {"comment":"Unit and drive"},
        "3559": {"comment":"Its unit"},
        "3564": {"comment":"Same unit?"},
        "3565": {"comment":"rc_partopen"},
        "3569": {"synopsis":"The next drive, up to 15.","comment":"Next drive"},
        "3571": {"comment":"16 drives"},
        "3575": {"comment":"D = the unit, E = drive + 1"},
        "3577": {"comment":"Descriptors: $2A10 + 53 x drive"},
        "3584": {"synopsis":"53 bytes per drive."},
        "3589": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "3590": {"comment":"Mount partition BC"},
        "3593": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "3595": {"comment":"E = drive + 1"},
        "3596": {"comment":"Records: $2D60 + 15 x drive"},
        "3603": {"synopsis":"15 bytes per drive."},
        "3608": {"comment":"The record at the root"},
        "3611": {"comment":"The drive's word"},
        "3612": {"comment":"= the record"},
        "3619": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3620": {"synopsis":"IX restored.","comment":"Restored"},
        "3623": {"synopsis":"Unmaps drive A (the vector at $0121, reached from the jump at $016C by IDE_DOS_UNMAP in\nROM 2): error $24 (rc_inuse) while one of the 17 six-byte entries at $2EB4 with bit 7 of\nits first byte set names the drive in its last byte, or an open file handle (16 of 45\nbytes at $2740, byte $0F not 0) is on the drive's descriptor. Otherwise the drive's word\nin the table at $2E6E is cleared.\nEntry: A = the drive 0-15.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = $24.","comment":"The table at $2EB4"},
        "3626": {"comment":"17 entries"},
        "3628": {"synopsis":"One entry of the table at $2EB4.","comment":"In use?"},
        "3633": {"comment":"Its last byte"},
        "3637": {"comment":"This drive?"},
        "3641": {"synopsis":"The next entry, 6 bytes on.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "3647": {"comment":"HL = the drive's word"},
        "3651": {"comment":"DE = its record's descriptor"},
        "3655": {"comment":"The file handles"},
        "3659": {"comment":"16"},
        "3661": {"synopsis":"One file handle.","comment":"Open?"},
        "3667": {"comment":"Its descriptor"},
        "3673": {"comment":"On this drive?"},
        "3677": {"synopsis":"In use: A = $24, carry clear.","comment":"Drop the word"},
        "3678": {"comment":"rc_inuse"},
        "3681": {"synopsis":"The next handle, 45 bytes on.","comment":"Next handle"},
        "3690": {"comment":"The drive's word"},
        "3691": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "3695": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3697": {"synopsis":"The text of drive A's mapping at BC (the vector at $011E, used by IDE_DOS_MAPPING in ROM\n2): the unit digit, '>', then the first 16 bytes of the partition's entry (PART_ENTRY_READ:\nthe slot digit, '>', the label and three spaces), and $FF. The drive's word at $2E6E is\nnot tested here.\nEntry: A = the drive 0-15, BC = the buffer.\nExit: carry set, A = the unit (bit 1 of IX+$10 cleared), BC = the partition, DE = the\n$FF's address; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"DE = the drive's record"},
        "3701": {"comment":"DE = its descriptor"},
        "3704": {"comment":"IY = it"},
        "3707": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "3710": {"comment":"Without the block-address bit"},
        "3713": {"comment":"As a digit"},
        "3717": {"comment":"Then '>'"},
        "3721": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "3722": {"comment":"The buffer stacked"},
        "3723": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3726": {"comment":"BC = the partition number"},
        "3728": {"comment":"Its entry at $2200"},
        "3736": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "3737": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "3738": {"comment":"The partition kept"},
        "3739": {"comment":"16 bytes of the entry"},
        "3744": {"comment":"Then $FF"},
        "3748": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "3752": {"synopsis":"DOS_FLUSH (the vector at $011B): each open file handle (byte $0F not 0) is brought up to\ndate by $16BF, then the sector cache written out ($08D1). The drive passed in A is not\nlooked at: every handle is done.\nExit: as $08D1. IX and IY kept.","comment":"Kept"},
        "3756": {"comment":"16 handles"},
        "3758": {"synopsis":"One handle."},
        "3759": {"comment":"Handle B - 1"},
        "3761": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "3764": {"comment":"Open?"},
        "3768": {"comment":"Write its state out"},
        "3771": {"comment":"Next"},
        "3778": {"comment":"The cache out"},
        "3781": {"synopsis":"On a FAT32 volume with an FSInfo sector (bit 6 of IX+$13), copies the free count and the\nnext-free hint (IX+$2B, 8 bytes) to its bytes $1E8-$1EF in the cache and marks the sector\nfor writing ($08E2).\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error. BC, DE, HL kept.","comment":"FSInfo in use?"},
        "3785": {"comment":"No: nothing to do"},
        "3790": {"comment":"DE = its sector"},
        "3794": {"comment":"High word 0"},
        "3797": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "3800": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "3802": {"comment":"Its free count at $1E8"},
        "3807": {"comment":"From IX+$2B"},
        "3814": {"comment":"8 bytes"},
        "3819": {"comment":"Mark the sector changed"},
        "3822": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3823": {"synopsis":"BC, DE and HL restored."},
        "3827": {"synopsis":"IDE_DRIVE (the vector at $0103): IX = 0, no handle for a unit.","comment":"No unit handle"},
        "3832": {"synopsis":"IDE_CAPACITY (the vector at $0106): IX = $00FC, then ROM2_SD_SIZE.","comment":"Passed to SD_CAPACITY"},
        "3836": {"synopsis":"Runs ROM 2's $17DE (SD_CAPACITY: the size of SD card C from its CSD register) through\n$03F8: NextReg $8E = 2 and the RET at $1FF9 leave the DivMMC memory; $3CFC there brings\nit back. Also from $0A43, which ORs the B it returns (2 for a block-addressed card) into\nIX+$10.\nEntry: C = the card, 0 or 1.\nExit: as SD_CAPACITY: carry set and DE:HL = the size in 512-byte sectors; or carry clear.","comment":"ROM 2's SD_CAPACITY"},
        "3839": {"comment":"Run it in ROM 2"},
        "3842": {"synopsis":"The label 'NO NAME' padded to 11 bytes with spaces: $0A5D's answer for a volume whose boot\nsector has no extended signature."},
        "3853": {"synopsis":"The checksum of the 11-byte short name at HL that ties long-name entries to it: each byte\nadded to the sum rotated right.\nExit: A = the checksum. HL kept; B = 0."},
        "3854": {"comment":"Sum 0"},
        "3855": {"comment":"11 bytes"},
        "3857": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Rotated right, plus the byte"},
        "3860": {"comment":"Next"},
        "3864": {"synopsis":"Takes the 13 characters of the long-name entry at HL, last first, into the text that ends\nat DE (bytes $1C-$1F, $0E-$19, $01-$0A of the entry, two bytes each): a character 0 or\n$FFFF is left out; one not in $20-$7E becomes '_'.\nExit: DE = the text's new start.","comment":"The entry's last byte"},
        "3868": {"comment":"Characters 12-13"},
        "3873": {"comment":"Skip bytes $1A-$1B"},
        "3875": {"comment":"Characters 6-11"},
        "3880": {"comment":"Skip bytes $0B-$0D"},
        "3883": {"comment":"Characters 1-5"},
        "3885": {"synopsis":"One 16-bit character, high byte first.","comment":"A = the high byte"},
        "3887": {"comment":"C = the low byte"},
        "3889": {"comment":"High byte 0?"},
        "3892": {"comment":"$FFFF: padding"},
        "3894": {"comment":"Leave it out"},
        "3896": {"comment":"Otherwise '_'"},
        "3898": {"synopsis":"High byte 0: the low byte as it is unless 0.","comment":"The low byte"},
        "3900": {"comment":"0: the end"},
        "3902": {"comment":"A control code?"},
        "3906": {"comment":"Pushed to $E0 up"},
        "3912": {"synopsis":"'_' for a character that cannot be shown.","comment":"'_'"},
        "3914": {"synopsis":"Stored, DE back by one.","comment":"Stored backwards"},
        "3916": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"Next"},
        "3919": {"synopsis":"Puts B characters of the name at DE as 16-bit units at HL (a long-name entry's part):\nthe $FF end of the name as $0000, every unit after it $FFFF. C carries the state between\ncalls: 1 in the name, 0 past its end.\nExit: DE and HL past what was used; C as above.","comment":"Still in the name?"},
        "3921": {"comment":"No: $FFFF"},
        "3923": {"comment":"A character"},
        "3925": {"comment":"The $FF end?"},
        "3928": {"comment":"$0000"},
        "3934": {"synopsis":"A character: A back to it.","comment":"The character back"},
        "3935": {"synopsis":"A low, C high.","comment":"Low byte"},
        "3937": {"comment":"High byte: C (0, or $FF past the end)"},
        "3939": {"comment":"C to 1 or 0"},
        "3940": {"synopsis":"The next unit.","comment":"Next"},
        "3943": {"synopsis":"Makes the 11-byte short name (8 + 3, padded with spaces, $FF after it) at DE for the\n$FF-ended long name at HL.\n1. Leading spaces and dots are skipped.\n2. Up to 8 characters of the base (SHORT_NAME_CHARS), then the extension: 3 characters\nafter the last dot.\n3. When something was lost (a character changed or dropped, a part too long), '~1' goes\nafter the base at its first space, at most at position 6.\nEntry: HL = the long name, DE = the buffer.\nExit: C = 0 for a faithful name; or C = 1, HL = the '1' of '~1' and B = the room for\ndigits (the state SHORT_TAIL_NEXT takes).","comment":"The buffer kept"},
        "3944": {"comment":"B = 11, C = 0: nothing lost"},
        "3948": {"synopsis":"A leading space or dot skipped.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "3950": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "3954": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3958": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "3962": {"comment":"The base: 8"},
        "3964": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "3967": {"comment":"The name ended"},
        "3969": {"comment":"Base padded"},
        "3972": {"comment":"The extension: 3"},
        "3974": {"comment":"Its dot found"},
        "3976": {"comment":"Base too long: a dot after it?"},
        "3979": {"comment":"None: no extension"},
        "3981": {"synopsis":"One more dot looked for: HL after the last.","comment":"Another dot?"},
        "3987": {"comment":"Yes: keep looking"},
        "3990": {"synopsis":"HL = after the last dot.","comment":"After the last dot"},
        "3991": {"synopsis":"The extension's characters.","comment":"The extension copied"},
        "3994": {"comment":"All of it?"},
        "3996": {"comment":"No: lost"},
        "3998": {"synopsis":"The rest of the extension padded.","comment":"Padded"},
        "4001": {"synopsis":"$FF after the 11 bytes; '~1' if anything was lost.","comment":"Then $FF"},
        "4004": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "4005": {"comment":"A space in the first 7?"},
        "4007": {"synopsis":"One byte of the base."},
        "4015": {"comment":"None: B = 1"},
        "4016": {"synopsis":"HL = where the '~' would go.","comment":"HL = the space, or position 6"},
        "4017": {"comment":"Anything lost?"},
        "4018": {"comment":"No: C = 0"},
        "4021": {"synopsis":"'~1' at HL; C = 1 digit, HL at the digit.","comment":"'~'"},
        "4024": {"comment":"'1'"},
        "4026": {"comment":"One digit"},
        "4028": {"synopsis":"The name ended in the base: the 3 extension bytes padded too.","comment":"B + 3: the extension too"},
        "4031": {"synopsis":"B spaces, then the end.","comment":"All spaces"},
        "4036": {"synopsis":"The next short name when the last one exists already: the number after '~' goes up by 1;\nwhen it gets a digit more and there is no room to its right, the '~' moves one to the left.\nA name without a tail gets '~1' (carry clear: the exact name exists).\nEntry: HL = the last digit, C = the digits, B = the room for digits (SHORT_NAME_MAKE).\nExit: carry set and HL, B, C updated; or carry clear (A = $1B, rc_dirfull, at 6 digits).","comment":"A tail yet?"},
        "4040": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4042": {"synopsis":"One digit up, from the last.","comment":"The digit + 1"},
        "4044": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "4048": {"comment":"'0', carry to the left"},
        "4051": {"comment":"More digits?"},
        "4054": {"comment":"All carried"},
        "4056": {"comment":"Room for one more digit?"},
        "4060": {"synopsis":"A digit more: '1' and A zeros after the '~'.","comment":"One digit more"},
        "4062": {"comment":"'1' then zeros"},
        "4064": {"synopsis":"One '0'."},
        "4070": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4072": {"synopsis":"No room: the '~' moves left, unless there are 6 digits.","comment":"Six digits?"},
        "4075": {"comment":"rc_dirfull"},
        "4078": {"comment":"More room"},
        "4080": {"comment":"'~' one to the left"},
        "4085": {"synopsis":"The number went up: carry set.","comment":"Restored"},
        "4089": {"synopsis":"A space: left out, the name marked as changed (C = 1)."},
        "4091": {"synopsis":"Copies up to B characters from the long name at HL to DE for a short name: lower-case\nletters made upper case; a code below $20 or from $80, or + , ; = [ ] becomes '_'; spaces\nand dots that are not the last dot are left out; C = 1 when anything changed.\nExit: Z set at the name's $FF end; carry set at the last dot (HL after it); otherwise\n(B characters taken and more follow) NZ, carry clear, C = 1, HL at the next one.","comment":"Next character"},
        "4093": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "4096": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "4100": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "4104": {"comment":"A control code?"},
        "4106": {"comment":"$80 up?"},
        "4110": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "4114": {"comment":"','?"},
        "4118": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "4122": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "4126": {"comment":"'['?"},
        "4130": {"comment":"']'?"},
        "4134": {"comment":"Lower case?"},
        "4142": {"comment":"Made upper case"},
        "4146": {"synopsis":"A character not allowed: '_', C = 1.","comment":"'_'"},
        "4148": {"comment":"Changed"},
        "4150": {"synopsis":"The character stored; the next.","comment":"Stored"},
        "4152": {"comment":"Next"},
        "4154": {"comment":"One past the B"},
        "4156": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "4159": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "4163": {"comment":"The last one?"},
        "4168": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "4169": {"synopsis":"More than B characters: NZ, carry clear, C = 1.","comment":"Back to it"},
        "4170": {"comment":"NZ, carry clear"},
        "4172": {"comment":"Too long: changed"},
        "4175": {"synopsis":"A dot: the extension's when no other follows; otherwise dropped.","comment":"A later dot?"},
        "4180": {"comment":"No: the extension's"},
        "4181": {"comment":"Dropped: changed"},
        "4185": {"synopsis":"Looks from HL for a dot before the $FF end.\nExit: carry clear and HL after the dot; or carry set, A = $FE, HL after the $FF.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "4187": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "4191": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "4196": {"synopsis":"No dot: carry set.","comment":"None: A = $FE"},
        "4199": {"synopsis":"Copies the name of the directory entry at record IY to DE: the long name gathered by\nDIR_ENTRY_FIND (bit 7 of IY+$0D) from ($2F26) up to and with its $FF at $302C; otherwise\nthe short name with a dot (SHORT_NAME_DOT).\nExit: DE after the $FF.","comment":"The destination"},
        "4200": {"comment":"A long name?"},
        "4206": {"comment":"Its start"},
        "4210": {"comment":"Up to $302C, its $FF"},
        "4218": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "4219": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "4223": {"synopsis":"No long name: the entry's short name.","comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "4227": {"synopsis":"The 11-byte short name at HL as text at DE: the base without its trailing spaces, '.', the\nextension without them (the '.' left out when there is none), then $FF. Also from $1C62.\nExit: carry set, DE after the $FF.","comment":"The base"},
        "4232": {"comment":"A dot"},
        "4236": {"comment":"The extension"},
        "4241": {"comment":"The last byte"},
        "4243": {"comment":"The dot?"},
        "4247": {"comment":"No: keep it"},
        "4248": {"synopsis":"The $FF end.","comment":"Then $FF"},
        "4252": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4254": {"synopsis":"Copies B bytes from HL to DE with bit 7 cleared, then moves DE back over the trailing\nspaces.","comment":"Trailing spaces 0"},
        "4256": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"The byte, bit 7 off"},
        "4260": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "4262": {"comment":"One more space"},
        "4263": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "4267": {"comment":"No: none trailing"},
        "4269": {"synopsis":"The next byte.","comment":"Next"},
        "4271": {"comment":"Any trailing?"},
        "4274": {"comment":"DE back over them"},
        "4280": {"synopsis":"Stores B spaces at DE (none for B = 0).","comment":"A space"},
        "4282": {"comment":"B = 0?"},
        "4283": {"synopsis":"One space."},
        "4285": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "4289": {"synopsis":"IY = the working directory record at $2E50, IX = its volume's descriptor (its first word).\nA directory record is 15 bytes: +0 the descriptor; +2 bit 7 the FAT16 root area; +3 the\ndirectory's first cluster (4 bytes); +7 the sector in the cluster; +8 the cluster (or the\nroot area's sector); +$0C the entry in the sector, 0-15; +$0D and +$0E the long-name state.","comment":"The working record"},
        "4293": {"comment":"Its descriptor"},
        "4298": {"synopsis":"Sets the directory record IY to the start of the root directory of the volume IX: the\ndescriptor stored, then FAT16's root area (bit 7 of IY+2, cluster 0) or FAT32's root\ncluster (IX+$1D), then DIR_REC_REWIND.\nExit: carry set. BC, DE kept.","comment":"The descriptor"},
        "4308": {"comment":"FAT16?"},
        "4314": {"comment":"FAT32: a cluster chain"},
        "4320": {"comment":"BCDE = the root cluster"},
        "4324": {"comment":"The first cluster"},
        "4332": {"synopsis":"FAT16: the fixed root area, first cluster 0.","comment":"The root area"},
        "4336": {"comment":"Cluster 0"},
        "4343": {"synopsis":"Moves the directory record IY back to its first entry: the current cluster (IY+8) = the\nfirst (IY+3), sector and entry 0.\nExit: carry set. BC, DE kept."},
        "4345": {"comment":"BCDE = the first cluster"},
        "4347": {"comment":"As the current one"},
        "4353": {"comment":"Sector 0"},
        "4357": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "4360": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4362": {"synopsis":"Moves the directory record IY into the directory whose entry it is at: its cluster (the\nhigh word from +$14 on FAT32) as the first; cluster 0 (a '..' to the root) gives\nDIR_REC_ROOT. Then DIR_REC_REWIND.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error, $45 (rc_notdir) for a free entry or a\nfile.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4365": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4366": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "4368": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "4372": {"comment":"Its cluster's low word"},
        "4379": {"comment":"High word 0"},
        "4382": {"comment":"FAT16?"},
        "4388": {"comment":"FAT32: the high word"},
        "4395": {"synopsis":"BCDE = the cluster: 0 means the root.","comment":"Cluster 0?"},
        "4399": {"comment":"Yes: the root"},
        "4401": {"comment":"The first cluster"},
        "4405": {"comment":"A cluster chain"},
        "4411": {"synopsis":"Not a directory: A = $45, carry clear."},
        "4415": {"synopsis":"Moves the directory record IY to its next entry: the next of 16 in the sector; then the\nnext sector, of FAT16's root area (up to IX+$1B) or of the cluster chain ($0577 with the\nfields at IY+7).\nExit: carry set; or carry clear at the end, A = $17 (the root area) or $19 (the chain's\nend), or another error.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "4418": {"comment":"16 done?"},
        "4422": {"comment":"No: success"},
        "4424": {"comment":"The root area?"},
        "4430": {"synopsis":"The next sector of the chain (fields at IY+7 and IY+8); entry 0.","comment":"Next sector or cluster"},
        "4433": {"comment":"End or error"},
        "4437": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "4442": {"synopsis":"FAT16's root area: the next of its IX+$1B sectors.","comment":"BC = the sector index"},
        "4444": {"comment":"+1"},
        "4445": {"comment":"The root area's sectors - 1"},
        "4453": {"comment":"Beyond?"},
        "4455": {"comment":"$17"},
        "4457": {"comment":"Carry clear if beyond"},
        "4459": {"comment":"The new index"},
        "4465": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "4470": {"synopsis":"Reads the sector of the directory record IY's entry into the cache: FAT16's root area sector\nIX+$1D + IY+8, or sector IY+7 of cluster IY+8 ($06EE).\nExit: carry set and HL = the 32-byte entry; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The root area?"},
        "4476": {"comment":"BCDE = the cluster"},
        "4478": {"comment":"The sector in it"},
        "4481": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "4484": {"synopsis":"HL = the buffer: the entry's address in it.","comment":"Read error"},
        "4485": {"comment":"The entry number"},
        "4490": {"comment":"x 32"},
        "4496": {"comment":"Plus the buffer"},
        "4499": {"synopsis":"FAT16's root area: its sector IY+8.","comment":"The root area's sector"},
        "4505": {"comment":"+ the index"},
        "4511": {"comment":"The carry to the high word"},
        "4518": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "4523": {"synopsis":"Reads the directory record IY's entry (DIR_ENTRY_ADDR).\nExit: carry set and HL = the entry; Z set for a free entry (first byte 0 or $E5, A = it);\notherwise B = its first byte, A = its attributes, C = byte $0D (a long-name entry's\nchecksum). Carry clear and A = the error when it cannot be read.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4526": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4527": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "4528": {"comment":"0: never used"},
        "4531": {"comment":"$E5: deleted"},
        "4536": {"comment":"B = the first byte"},
        "4541": {"comment":"A = the attributes"},
        "4544": {"comment":"C = byte $0D"},
        "4546": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4548": {"synopsis":"Finds E free entries in a row in the directory of record IY, from its start: the record is\nleft at the first of them. At the end of the chain a new cluster is linked on ($063E),\ncleared ($0688) and written ($08D1); FAT16's root area cannot grow.\nEntry: E = the entries wanted.\nExit: carry set and HL = the first entry (DIR_ENTRY_READ); or carry clear and A = the\nerror.","comment":"From the start"},
        "4551": {"comment":"None in a row yet"},
        "4554": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4558": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4559": {"comment":"Used?"},
        "4561": {"comment":"The first of a row?"},
        "4566": {"comment":"Its position kept at $201A"},
        "4572": {"synopsis":"One more free entry in the row: enough?","comment":"One more"},
        "4574": {"comment":"Enough?"},
        "4579": {"synopsis":"A used entry: the row starts again.","comment":"Used: none in a row"},
        "4581": {"synopsis":"The next entry; at the chain's end a new cluster.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "4585": {"comment":"There is one"},
        "4587": {"comment":"The root area: full"},
        "4593": {"comment":"BCDE = the last cluster"},
        "4595": {"comment":"A new one linked on"},
        "4598": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "4601": {"comment":"The cache out"},
        "4604": {"comment":"Moved into it"},
        "4609": {"synopsis":"The directory cannot grow: carry clear."},
        "4611": {"synopsis":"Enough: the record back at the row's first entry.","comment":"Back to the first of the row"},
        "4617": {"comment":"Its entry"},
        "4619": {"synopsis":"HL = IY+7, DE = $201A, BC = 6: the arguments for an LDIR that keeps (or with HL and DE\nswapped restores) a directory record's position (bytes 7-12).","comment":"HL = IY+7"},
        "4626": {"comment":"The copy at $201A"},
        "4629": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "4633": {"synopsis":"Looks through the root directory of volume IX, in the working record $2E50, for the volume\nlabel: an entry with attribute bit 3 set, bit 4 clear, that is not a long-name part.\nExit: carry set; Z set and HL = the entry when found, NZ when not (A = 1); or carry clear\nand A = the error.","comment":"The working record"},
        "4637": {"comment":"At the root"},
        "4641": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4644": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4645": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "4647": {"comment":"Attributes"},
        "4650": {"comment":"A long-name part?"},
        "4654": {"comment":"A label, not a directory?"},
        "4659": {"comment":"Found: carry and Z"},
        "4661": {"synopsis":"The next entry; none left gives NZ.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "4664": {"comment":"There is one"},
        "4666": {"comment":"None: NZ"},
        "4668": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "4670": {"synopsis":"Finds the first used short-name entry from the directory record IY's position on, gathering\nthe long name before it (DFIND_NEXT does the same from the next entry):\n1. A long-name part with bit 6 of its number (the last part, which comes first) starts the\nname: the count at IY+$0D, the checksum at IY+$0E, the position kept at $2020, $FF at\n$302C, its characters before it (LFN_ENTRY_TAKE; start at ($2F26)).\n2. Each further part must carry the next lower number and the same checksum; anything else\nstarts again.\n3. A volume label is passed over. At a short-name entry, IY+$0D = $FF when all parts came\nand the checksum of its name (LFN_CHECKSUM) matches; otherwise 0.\nExit: carry set, HL = the entry, E = its attributes; or carry clear and A = the error, $17\nat a first byte 0 (the end).","comment":"No long name yet"},
        "4676": {"synopsis":"Start again from the next entry.","comment":"No long name yet"},
        "4680": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "4683": {"comment":"The end or an error"},
        "4684": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4687": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4688": {"comment":"Used?"},
        "4690": {"comment":"Deleted: skip"},
        "4693": {"comment":"0: the end, rc_nofile"},
        "4696": {"synopsis":"A used entry: a long-name part or a short name.","comment":"E = the attributes"},
        "4697": {"comment":"A long-name part?"},
        "4703": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "4704": {"comment":"The last part?"},
        "4708": {"comment":"The number expected"},
        "4711": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "4716": {"comment":"Its checksum"},
        "4717": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "4722": {"comment":"Where the text starts"},
        "4726": {"synopsis":"The part's characters added before the text; the next entry.","comment":"Its characters before it"},
        "4729": {"comment":"The new start"},
        "4735": {"synopsis":"The last part (first met): a new long name of A parts.","comment":"The parts"},
        "4737": {"comment":"More than 20?"},
        "4741": {"comment":"The count"},
        "4744": {"comment":"The checksum"},
        "4747": {"comment":"The entry kept"},
        "4748": {"comment":"The position"},
        "4751": {"comment":"Kept at $2020"},
        "4757": {"comment":"The text's end"},
        "4760": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "4765": {"synopsis":"A short-name entry: is the long name complete?","comment":"The attributes"},
        "4766": {"comment":"A volume label?"},
        "4772": {"comment":"All the parts there?"},
        "4775": {"comment":"The count cleared"},
        "4779": {"comment":"No: no long name"},
        "4781": {"comment":"The checksum"},
        "4784": {"comment":"Its parts'?"},
        "4787": {"comment":"No: no long name"},
        "4789": {"comment":"$FF: a long name"},
        "4793": {"synopsis":"Directory-record calls (the vector at $0127) chosen by B, on the working record $2E50\n(WORK_DIR_SELECT):\n1. B = 1: drive A's record copied to $2E50 ($0A1A), at its first entry; HL = $2E50,\nA = 15. From $02F4, setting the default drive.\n2. B = 2: $2E50 copied back to drive A's record ($0A0A).\n3. B = 3: $2E50 to the root (DIR_REC_ROOT).\n4. B = 4: $2E50 copied to $2E5F.\n5. B = 5: into the directory at $2E50's entry (DIR_ENTER_SUB).\n6. Another B: A = $3A (rc_notimp) through $0014.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The working record"},
        "4796": {"comment":"B = 1?"},
        "4798": {"comment":"Drive A's record to it"},
        "4801": {"comment":"At its first entry"},
        "4804": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "4807": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "4810": {"synopsis":"B = 2: the working record copied to drive A's.","comment":"B = 2?"},
        "4812": {"comment":"IY = drive A's record"},
        "4815": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "4818": {"comment":"From the working record"},
        "4828": {"synopsis":"B = 3: the root; B = 4: a copy at $2E5F.","comment":"B = 3?"},
        "4829": {"comment":"The working record to the root"},
        "4832": {"comment":"B = 4?"},
        "4834": {"comment":"The working record"},
        "4837": {"comment":"Copied to $2E5F"},
        "4847": {"synopsis":"B = 5: into the directory at the entry; others rc_notimp.","comment":"B = 5?"},
        "4848": {"comment":"Into the directory"},
        "4851": {"comment":"Not implemented"},
        "4854": {"synopsis":"Puts the first cluster of record IY's directory (0 for the root, DIR_AT_ROOT) into the\nsecond 32-byte entry from HL, the '..' of a new directory: its low word at +$3A, the high\nword at +$34.\nEntry: HL = the new directory's first entry.\nExit: IX kept.","comment":"The entries"},
        "4855": {"comment":"The root?"},
        "4858": {"comment":"IX = the entries"},
        "4860": {"comment":"Cluster 0"},
        "4866": {"comment":"The root: 0"},
        "4868": {"comment":"BCDE = the first cluster"},
        "4870": {"synopsis":"BCDE into the '..' entry.","comment":"Low word at '..'+$1A"},
        "4876": {"comment":"High word at '..'+$14"},
        "4885": {"synopsis":"Is the directory of record IY the root of volume IX? FAT16: bit 7 of IY+2; FAT32: its first\ncluster IY+3 the same as the root cluster IX+$1D.\nExit: carry set for the root. BC, DE, HL kept.","comment":"FAT16?"},
        "4894": {"comment":"BCDE = the root cluster"},
        "4900": {"comment":"BCDE = the record's"},
        "4902": {"comment":"Low words the same?"},
        "4906": {"comment":"High words the same?"},
        "4911": {"synopsis":"Z set when they are the same."},
        "4914": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "4916": {"comment":"No: carry clear"},
        "4918": {"synopsis":"FAT16: bit 7 of IY+2.","comment":"The root area?"},
        "4922": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "4924": {"comment":"No: carry clear"},
        "4926": {"synopsis":"Is the first cluster of the entry at HL BCDE (low word at +$1A, high at +$14)?\nExit: Z set when it is.","comment":"The low word"},
        "4932": {"comment":"Low byte?"},
        "4935": {"comment":"High byte?"},
        "4937": {"comment":"The high word"},
        "4943": {"comment":"Byte 3?"},
        "4946": {"comment":"Byte 2?"},
        "4948": {"synopsis":"Selects file handle A: IY = $2740 + 45 x A, IX = its volume's descriptor (its first word).\nA handle starts with the 15-byte directory record of its entry; +$0F the mode (bit 0 read,\nbit 1 write, bit 6 the position below valid, bit 7 the entry to update); +$10 the sector\nin the cluster; +$11 the cluster; +$15 the byte in the sector; +$17 the file pointer;\n+$1B the first cluster; +$1F the size (4 bytes each).\nExit: B = 0. DE kept.","comment":"B = the handle"},
        "4949": {"synopsis":"HANDLE_SELECT for handle B (from $1760).","comment":"Kept"},
        "4950": {"comment":"One before handle 0"},
        "4957": {"comment":"B + 1 steps"},
        "4958": {"synopsis":"45 bytes per handle."},
        "4962": {"comment":"IX = the descriptor"},
        "4974": {"synopsis":"Is the file at directory record IY in use? (From $171D.)\n1. An open handle (+$0F not 0) whose first 15 bytes are the same record: NZ, carry clear,\nHL = the handle.\n2. Otherwise the file's first sector as the card address ($06C3, $1EC8): when one of the 17\nentries at $2EB4 has it, with the unit + $80 in its first byte: A = 3, carry clear.\nExit: carry set when not in use; or carry clear (as above, or A = a read error).","comment":"16 handles"},
        "4976": {"comment":"From handle 0"},
        "4979": {"synopsis":"One handle."},
        "4981": {"comment":"DE = the record"},
        "4985": {"comment":"15 bytes"},
        "4987": {"synopsis":"One byte of the record.","comment":"The same?"},
        "4995": {"comment":"Open?"},
        "4999": {"comment":"Yes: HL = the handle"},
        "5002": {"synopsis":"The next handle."},
        "5004": {"comment":"Next handle"},
        "5010": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "5014": {"comment":"DE = the cluster's high word"},
        "5021": {"comment":"BC = its low word"},
        "5028": {"comment":"Sector 0 of it"},
        "5032": {"comment":"As the card's address"},
        "5035": {"comment":"BC = its high word"},
        "5037": {"comment":"17 entries"},
        "5042": {"synopsis":"One six-byte entry at $2EB4."},
        "5046": {"comment":"In use, and on this unit?"},
        "5055": {"comment":"Its address"},
        "5062": {"comment":"High words the same?"},
        "5068": {"comment":"Low words the same?"},
        "5076": {"comment":"Found"},
        "5080": {"comment":"A = 3"},
        "5083": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "5094": {"comment":"Not in use"},
        "5096": {"synopsis":"Is the file pointer of handle IY (+$17) below its size (+$1F)?\nExit: carry set when it is.","comment":"BCDE = the pointer"},
        "5100": {"comment":"BCDE = the size"},
        "5102": {"comment":"Pointer - size"},
        "5107": {"comment":"The high words"},
        "5110": {"synopsis":"Before a byte is written at handle IY's pointer: at or past the end, the size becomes the\npointer + 1.","comment":"Inside the file?"},
        "5114": {"comment":"DE:HL = the pointer"},
        "5117": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "5127": {"synopsis":"The size of handle IY = DE:HL.","comment":"BC = the low word"},
        "5129": {"comment":"The size"},
        "5148": {"synopsis":"Moves handle IY's pointer on by 1; with a valid position (bit 6 of +$0F) the byte in the\nsector too, and at 512 the next sector ($0577 on the fields at +$10). At the chain's end\nthe position is marked not valid.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The pointer + 1"},
        "5166": {"synopsis":"The position, when valid.","comment":"A valid position?"},
        "5170": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "5172": {"comment":"The byte in the sector + 1"},
        "5179": {"comment":"512?"},
        "5184": {"comment":"Byte 0"},
        "5188": {"comment":"Next sector or cluster"},
        "5194": {"comment":"Done"},
        "5195": {"comment":"Position not valid"},
        "5199": {"comment":"The chain's end?"},
        "5201": {"comment":"No: carry clear"},
        "5205": {"synopsis":"Moves handle IY's pointer on by BC; with a valid position, the byte in the sector too,\n512 at a time into the next sector ($0577). A BC with bit 7 set, or the chain's end, marks\nthe position not valid.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The pointer + BC"},
        "5220": {"comment":"The carry to its high word"},
        "5228": {"synopsis":"The position, when valid.","comment":"A valid position?"},
        "5234": {"comment":"BC from $8000?"},
        "5238": {"comment":"The byte in the sector + BC"},
        "5251": {"synopsis":"HL = the byte in the sector: a whole sector past it?","comment":"512 or more?"},
        "5258": {"comment":"Less 512"},
        "5264": {"comment":"Next sector or cluster"},
        "5270": {"comment":"The chain's end?"},
        "5272": {"comment":"Again with the rest"},
        "5280": {"synopsis":"No next sector: carry set at the chain's end, clear on an error.","comment":"The chain's end?"},
        "5285": {"comment":"No: carry clear"},
        "5286": {"synopsis":"The position marked not valid.","comment":"Position not valid"},
        "5291": {"synopsis":"The card position of handle IY's pointer.\n1. A valid position (bit 6 of +$0F) is used as it is.\n2. Otherwise from the first cluster (+$1B; a file without one gets a new cluster, $05BF):\none link of the chain per cluster's bytes in the pointer, the chain extended ($063E)\npast its end; the rest gives the sector (+$10) and the byte (+$15); bit 6 set.\nExit: carry set, BCDE = the sector ($06C3), HL = the byte in it; or carry clear and A = the\nerror.","comment":"A valid position?"},
        "5297": {"comment":"BCDE = the first cluster"},
        "5299": {"comment":"A cluster?"},
        "5304": {"comment":"None: a new one"},
        "5308": {"comment":"As the first"},
        "5312": {"synopsis":"BCDE = the first cluster: the current one.","comment":"As the current one"},
        "5316": {"comment":"DE:HL = the pointer"},
        "5319": {"comment":"BC = 256 x sectors per cluster"},
        "5324": {"synopsis":"One cluster's bytes off the pointer, in two halves.","comment":"Half a cluster's bytes off"},
        "5329": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "5333": {"comment":"Borrow from the high word"},
        "5334": {"synopsis":"The second half.","comment":"The other half"},
        "5338": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "5342": {"comment":"Borrow"},
        "5343": {"synopsis":"A whole cluster passed: the next cluster of the chain.","comment":"A whole cluster: the next"},
        "5346": {"comment":"BCDE = the current cluster"},
        "5348": {"comment":"Its link"},
        "5353": {"comment":"A cluster?"},
        "5358": {"comment":"The chain's end: link a new one"},
        "5365": {"synopsis":"The new current cluster.","comment":"The current cluster"},
        "5374": {"synopsis":"An error: the stacked words dropped."},
        "5378": {"synopsis":"Back over two halves.","comment":"Both halves back"},
        "5379": {"synopsis":"Back over one half: HL = the byte in the cluster.","comment":"One half back"},
        "5380": {"comment":"Bytes per sector"},
        "5384": {"synopsis":"One sector's 512 bytes.","comment":"Count the sectors"},
        "5389": {"comment":"HL = the rest"},
        "5391": {"comment":"The sector in the cluster"},
        "5394": {"comment":"The byte in the sector"},
        "5400": {"comment":"Position valid"},
        "5404": {"synopsis":"The valid position: its sector and byte.","comment":"BCDE = the cluster"},
        "5406": {"comment":"The sector in it"},
        "5409": {"comment":"Its card sector"},
        "5412": {"comment":"HL = the byte"},
        "5419": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of the byte at handle IY's pointer, its sector read into the cache\n(FILE_POS_SECTOR, then $0832).\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The sector and byte"},
        "5422": {"comment":"Error"},
        "5423": {"synopsis":"FILE_BYTE_ADDR with BCDE and HL from FILE_POS_SECTOR.","comment":"The byte kept"},
        "5424": {"comment":"The sector read"},
        "5429": {"comment":"HL = the byte's address"},
        "5432": {"synopsis":"DOS_BYTE_READ (the vector at $0148): the byte at handle A's pointer, the pointer moved on.\nExit: carry set, C = the byte, Z set when it is $1A (soft end of file); or carry clear and\nA = the error: $1D (rc_number) when the handle is not open for reading, $19 (rc_eof) at the\nend.","comment":"The handle"},
        "5435": {"comment":"Open for reading?"},
        "5441": {"comment":"Inside the file?"},
        "5446": {"comment":"The byte's address"},
        "5451": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "5453": {"comment":"The pointer + 1"},
        "5457": {"comment":"C = the byte"},
        "5458": {"comment":"$1A?"},
        "5460": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5462": {"synopsis":"Not open that way: A = $1D.","comment":"rc_number"},
        "5466": {"synopsis":"At the end: A = $19.","comment":"rc_eof"},
        "5468": {"synopsis":"Carry clear.","comment":"Carry clear"},
        "5470": {"synopsis":"DOS_BYTE_WRITE (the vector at $014B): the byte C at handle A's pointer, the size grown\nwhen it is at the end (FILE_SIZE_GROW), the sector marked for writing ($08E2), the pointer\nmoved on.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error ($1D when not open for writing).","comment":"The handle"},
        "5473": {"comment":"Open for writing?"},
        "5479": {"comment":"The byte kept"},
        "5480": {"comment":"The size grown"},
        "5483": {"comment":"The byte's address"},
        "5487": {"comment":"Error"},
        "5489": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5490": {"comment":"The sector changed"},
        "5493": {"comment":"The pointer + 1"},
        "5496": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5498": {"synopsis":"Reads DE bytes from handle A's pointer to HL (the vector at $0142; ROM 2's READ_BLOCK).\n1. C without bit 7: 16K bank C is paged at $C000 (MMU 6 and 7, $0087) and bank 7 put back\nat the end ($0082).\n2. Not open for reading: $1D; at or past the end: $19. The count is cut to what is left of\nthe file ($200D); the bytes still wanted are at $200B, the destination at $2009.\n3. A sector at a time: a whole sector into a handle not open for writing goes straight\nfrom the card ($1EA5); otherwise it comes through the cache.\n4. Ending before all DE bytes were read gives $19.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear, A = the error and DE = the bytes not read.","comment":"The handle"},
        "5501": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "5504": {"comment":"The count"},
        "5508": {"comment":"The bank kept"},
        "5509": {"comment":"A bank to page?"},
        "5514": {"comment":"Open for reading?"},
        "5521": {"comment":"Inside the file?"},
        "5527": {"comment":"BCDE = the size"},
        "5530": {"comment":"HL = its low word"},
        "5532": {"comment":"BCDE = the pointer"},
        "5534": {"comment":"Size - pointer"},
        "5543": {"comment":"The count"},
        "5546": {"comment":"More than 65535 left?"},
        "5548": {"comment":"Count - what is left"},
        "5552": {"comment":"Count the smaller"},
        "5555": {"synopsis":"One sector's part, or one whole sector.","comment":"The bytes for this call"},
        "5558": {"comment":"Sector and byte"},
        "5561": {"comment":"Error"},
        "5563": {"comment":"Open for writing too?"},
        "5569": {"comment":"At the sector's start?"},
        "5573": {"comment":"512 or more to go?"},
        "5580": {"comment":"The whole sector"},
        "5583": {"comment":"Straight to the destination"},
        "5586": {"comment":"HL after it"},
        "5589": {"comment":"Error"},
        "5591": {"comment":"512 bytes done"},
        "5596": {"synopsis":"Through the cache: up to the sector's end, at most what is wanted.","comment":"The byte's address"},
        "5601": {"comment":"The bytes left in the sector"},
        "5609": {"comment":"The bytes still to read"},
        "5613": {"comment":"Fewer?"},
        "5617": {"comment":"BC = the smaller"},
        "5620": {"synopsis":"BC bytes copied to the destination."},
        "5621": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "5625": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "5627": {"comment":"Its new end"},
        "5632": {"synopsis":"BC bytes done: the counts and the pointer.","comment":"Wanted - done"},
        "5641": {"comment":"Z kept: all wanted done?"},
        "5643": {"comment":"The pointer + BC"},
        "5648": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "5650": {"comment":"This call's - done"},
        "5656": {"comment":"Nothing more in the file"},
        "5658": {"comment":"Again"},
        "5660": {"synopsis":"All done: bank 7 back if one was paged; carry set. Also from $1665.","comment":"The bank"},
        "5661": {"comment":"Paged?"},
        "5663": {"comment":"Bank 7 back"},
        "5666": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5668": {"synopsis":"Past the end: A = $19.","comment":"rc_eof"},
        "5672": {"synopsis":"Not open that way: A = $1D.","comment":"rc_number"},
        "5674": {"synopsis":"An error: bank 7 back if one was paged, carry clear, DE = the bytes not read.","comment":"The bank"},
        "5675": {"comment":"Paged?"},
        "5677": {"comment":"Bank 7 back"},
        "5680": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "5681": {"comment":"DE = the bytes not read"},
        "5686": {"synopsis":"Vector $0145 (ROM 2's WRITE_BLOCK): writes DE bytes from HL to file A at its position.\n1. IY = handle A (HANDLE_SELECT); with C bit 7 = 0, 16K bank C is paged at $C000 (MMU 6 and\n   7) for the source.\n2. Error $1D (rc_number) unless the file is open for writing.\n3. Each sector takes as many bytes as fit from the position: copied into the sector buffer,\n   which is marked changed; the size grows with the position (FILE_SIZE_GROW).\nExit: Fc=1 all written; Fc=0 A = error, DE = bytes not written.\nChanges: $2009 (source pointer), $200B (bytes left).","comment":"IY = handle A's record, IX its volume"},
        "5689": {"comment":"Source pointer"},
        "5692": {"comment":"Bytes left to write"},
        "5696": {"comment":"Keep C, the bank byte"},
        "5697": {"comment":"C bit 7 clear: bank C paged in at $C000"},
        "5702": {"comment":"Open for writing?"},
        "5708": {"synopsis":"One sector's part of the data.","comment":"HL = the position's byte in the sector buffer, DE its offset"},
        "5711": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5713": {"comment":"Keep the buffer address"},
        "5714": {"comment":"HL = room left in the sector ($200 - offset)"},
        "5720": {"comment":"DE = destination in the buffer"},
        "5721": {"comment":"BC = bytes left to write"},
        "5725": {"comment":"Do they all fit?"},
        "5729": {"comment":"No: BC = the room"},
        "5732": {"synopsis":"BC bytes into the sector buffer.","comment":"Keep the chunk's length"},
        "5733": {"comment":"Copy the chunk from the source"},
        "5738": {"comment":"Source pointer moved on"},
        "5741": {"comment":"Sector buffer changed"},
        "5744": {"comment":"BC = chunk length"},
        "5745": {"comment":"Bytes left reduced by it"},
        "5754": {"comment":"Keep Z: nothing left?"},
        "5755": {"comment":"Position + chunk - 1"},
        "5759": {"comment":"Size = position + 1 when passed"},
        "5762": {"comment":"Position + 1"},
        "5766": {"comment":"All written: out through BLK_DONE"},
        "5768": {"comment":"Next sector"},
        "5770": {"synopsis":"Vector $014E (ROM 2's DOS_GET_POSITION): the position of file A.\nExit: DEHL = the position, Fc=1.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5773": {"synopsis":"DEHL = the position (field $17) of the handle at IY; Fc=1.","comment":"BC, DE = position (low, high)"},
        "5775": {"comment":"HL = low word"},
        "5777": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5779": {"synopsis":"Vector $0151 (ROM 2's DOS_SET_POSITION): sets file A's position to DEHL, unchecked.\nExit: Fc=1.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5782": {"synopsis":"Sets the position (field $17) of the handle at IY to DEHL and clears bit 6 of +$0F, so that\nits cluster and sector are found again (FILE_POS_SECTOR).\nExit: Fc=1.","comment":"BC = low word"},
        "5784": {"comment":"Field $17 = the position"},
        "5788": {"comment":"Cluster and sector to be found again"},
        "5794": {"synopsis":"Vector $0154 (ROM 2's DOS_GET_EOF): file A's directory entry details.\nExit: Fc=1 with DEHL = the size, IX = the entry's time and BC its date (MS-DOS form); Fc=0\nwhen the entry cannot be read.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5797": {"comment":"HL = the file's directory entry"},
        "5800": {"comment":"Unreadable?"},
        "5801": {"comment":"Entry + $16: time, then date"},
        "5805": {"comment":"DE = time"},
