        "5836": {"synopsis":"Vector $0160: writes file A's state to the disk if it is open for writing:\n1. A +3DOS header written again (HEADER_WRITE) when the file has one.\n2. The buffers flushed ($08D1).\n3. The directory entry gets the archive bit, the first cluster, the time and date now and\n   the size, and its sector is written ($0853).\nExit: Fc=1 (also with nothing to do); Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5839": {"synopsis":"FILE_SYNC for the handle at IY (also from $0E9F).","comment":"Nothing to do: Fc=1"},
