        "5908": {"comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5911": {"comment":"Success; free the handle"},
        "5914": {"synopsis":"Vector $0157: changes file A's access mode to C: the file's state is written (FILE_SYNC_IY),\nthen mode C is checked and set as at open (ACCESS_CHECK).\nExit: Fc=1; Fc=0 A = error, the old mode kept.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5917": {"comment":"B = the current mode byte"},
        "5921": {"comment":"Write the file's state"},
        "5925": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5926": {"comment":"Mode 0 while the others are searched"},
        "5930": {"synopsis":"Checks access mode C for the file at IY against its other users and sets it. Mode bits: 0\nread, 1 write, 2 shared (1-3 exclusive, 5-7 shared: DOS_OPEN's access modes), 3 sharing not\nchecked; $10 and up refused.\n1. With +$0F = 0, the other handles and the list at $2EB4 are searched for the same file\n   (FILE_OPEN_CHECK).\n2. In use: allowed with bit 3; refused for an exclusive mode, for shared writing, or when\n   the other user writes without sharing.\n3. Write access to a read-only file: error $1C (rc_ro).\nEntry: B = the mode byte whose high nibble is kept.\nExit: Fc=1, +$0F = B's high nibble + C; Fc=0 A = $1E (rc_denied) or $1C.","comment":"Keep B and the mode"},
        "5931": {"comment":"16 handles"},
        "5933": {"comment":"Same file in use? (Fc=0, A = its mode)"},
        "5937": {"comment":"Mode byte back for now"},
        "5940": {"comment":"Not in use: check the mode"},
        "5942": {"comment":"Bit 3: sharing not checked"},
        "5946": {"comment":"Exclusive mode wanted: refused"},
        "5950": {"comment":"Shared writing wanted: refused"},
        "5954": {"comment":"Other user writes without sharing?"},
        "5960": {"synopsis":"The mode itself: a code below $10; write access only to a file that is not read-only.","comment":"A = the wanted mode"},
        "5961": {"comment":"$10 or more?"},
        "5965": {"comment":"Write access wanted?"},
        "5969": {"comment":"A = the entry's attributes"},
        "5974": {"comment":"Unreadable?"},
        "5975": {"comment":"Read-only file?"},
        "5977": {"comment":"rc_ro"},
        "5981": {"synopsis":"Mode byte = B's high nibble + C; Fc=1.","comment":"Keep the high nibble"},
        "5985": {"comment":"Set the mode"},
        "5988": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5990": {"synopsis":"Refused by the sharing test: A = $24 (rc_inuse) is replaced at once by $1E (ACCESS_DENIED).","comment":"rc_inuse, overwritten by the next load"},
        "5992": {"synopsis":"Error $1E (rc_denied): mode refused.","comment":"rc_denied"},
        "5994": {"synopsis":"Error exit with A kept: Fc=0.","comment":"Fc=0"},
        "5996": {"synopsis":"Vector $0136: opens as handle B the file found by the search record $2E50, or creates it.\nEntry: B = handle (0-15); C = access mode (ACCESS_CHECK); D bit 1 = 1 open the entry found,\n0 create one named by HL ($FF-ended, ENTRY_CREATE); D bit 0 = 0 for a +3DOS header (read\nfrom an existing file, written new in a created one); IX = an 8-byte buffer for the header's\nBASIC bytes, or 0.\n1. The handle filled from the search record and the entry (HANDLE_INIT).\n2. The access mode checked and set.\n3. The header dealt with.\nExit: Fc=1 open; Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"Header buffer address"},
        "6000": {"comment":"IY = handle B's record"},
