        "6165": {"synopsis":"Makes the directory entries for a new file named by HL ($FF-ended) in the search record's\ndirectory (IY = $2E50):\n1. '.' and '..' refused: error $14 (rc_badname).\n2. The 8.3 form at $202E (SHORT_NAME_MAKE); while an entry already has those 11 bytes, its\n   numeric tail is raised (SHORT_TAIL_NEXT).\n3. One long-name entry per 13 characters, 20 at most (else error $14), and that many plus\n   one free entries in a row (DIR_FREE_FIND).\n4. The long-name entries, from the name's last part: the ordinal (bit 6 on the first\n   written), 13 characters in 16 bits each, attribute $0F, the 8.3 name's checksum; then the\n   8.3 entry: the archive attribute, zeros, the time and date now.\nExit: Fc=1, the search record on the 8.3 entry; Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"Keep the name"},
        "6166": {"comment":"A = first character"},
