        "6486": {"synopsis":"Reads the +3DOS header of the file at IY:\n1. A file of 128 bytes or more has its first 128 checked (HEADER_CHECK).\n2. Valid: bit 7 of +$0F set; the size and the 8 BASIC header bytes taken from it into +$1F\n   and +$23, copied to the header buffer (HEADER_TO_USER); position 128.\n3. Otherwise HEADER_NONE makes one up.\nExit: Fc=1.","comment":"No header known yet"},
        "6490": {"comment":"DEHL = the size"},
