        "6633": {"synopsis":"The 11 bytes that start a +3DOS header: \"PLUS3DOS\", $1A, $01, $00. HEADER_WRITE writes them;\nHEADER_CHECK compares them."},
        "6644": {"synopsis":"Reads entries from the search record's position until one passes:\n1. One entry into the buffer at DE (vector $0139, DIR_ENTRY_GET).\n2. The attribute filter C (DIR_FILTER).\n3. With B bit 5, the name must match the pattern at HL (NAME_MATCH).\n4. Rejected: with B bit 1, CAPS SHIFT + SPACE stops the search; then the next entry (vector\n   $013C with A = 0).\nEntry: HL = pattern ($FF-ended), DE = buffer, B = options (bit 6 passed on to\nDIR_ENTRY_GET), C = filter.\nExit: Fc=1 an entry found, in the buffer; Fc=0 at the end, an error or BREAK.","comment":"Keep pattern, buffer, options"},
        "6647": {"comment":"Vector $0139: next entry to the buffer"},
