        "7840": {"synopsis":"Port $E3 = 0 (CONMEM off, RAM bank 0), then out through AUTOMAP_OFF_RET. From $006E.","comment":"CONMEM off, bank 0"},
        "7855": {"synopsis":"Reads sector BCDE of the device at IX (its record: +$01 first sector, +$07 size, +$10 flags)\nto HL, 512 bytes (SD_ADDRESS, SD_BLOCK_READ).\nExit: Fc=1, HL past the data; Fc=0 A = error (2 rc_seek: beyond the device; 0 rc_ready: the\ncard failed). BC, DE and IX kept."},
        "7856": {"synopsis":"Sector transfer for SD_SECTOR_READ (A = 0) and SD_SECTOR_WRITE (A = $80).","comment":"Keep BC, DE and the buffer"},
        "7859": {"comment":"HLDE = card address"},
        "7862": {"comment":"IX = buffer; device record kept"},
        "7864": {"comment":"Beyond the device?"},
        "7866": {"comment":"Keep the card choice (Z card 0)"},
        "7867": {"comment":"Write?"},
        "7872": {"comment":"Write the block"},
        "7877": {"synopsis":"Read the block."},
        "7878": {"comment":"Read the block"},
        "7881": {"synopsis":"IX, DE and BC back.","comment":"Device record back"},
        "7886": {"synopsis":"Writes sector BCDE of the device at IX from HL, 512 bytes (SD_TRANSFER with A = $80).\nExit: Fc=1; Fc=0 A = error (2 rc_seek beyond the device; 0 rc_ready, 1 rc_wp or 3 rc_crc\nfrom SD_BLOCK_WRITE).","comment":"A = $80: write"},
        "7890": {"synopsis":"Sector BCDE of the device record at IX as a card address:\n1. Error 2 (rc_seek) when BCDE is above the device's size (+$07).\n2. The device's first sector (+$01) added.\n3. x 512 when bit 1 of +$10 is 0 (a card addressed in bytes).\nExit: Fc=1, HLDE = the address, Z for card 0 (+$10 bit 0 = 0), NZ card 1; Fc=0 A = 2.","comment":"HL = size, low word"},
        "7896": {"comment":"Minus the sector"},
        "7899": {"comment":"Size, high word"},
        "7905": {"comment":"Sector beyond the size?"},
        "7909": {"comment":"rc_seek"},
        "7913": {"synopsis":"The device's first sector added.","comment":"First sector, low word"},
        "7919": {"comment":"DE = low word"},
        "7921": {"comment":"First sector, high word"},
        "7927": {"comment":"HL = high word"},
        "7929": {"comment":"Card addressed in blocks?"},
        "7935": {"comment":"No: x 256"},
        "7940": {"comment":"x 2"},
        "7945": {"synopsis":"Z or NZ: which card.","comment":"Card 1?"},
        "7949": {"comment":"Success"},
        "7951": {"synopsis":"SD_COMMAND with argument 0.","comment":"Argument 0"},
        "7957": {"synopsis":"Sends SPI command A with argument HLDE (high byte first) and $FF as CRC to card 0 (Z, port\n$E7 = $FE) or card 1 (NZ, $FD), then waits for the response (SD_WAIT_BYTE).\nExit: Fc=1 response 0; Fc=0 A = the response ($FF none).","comment":"CRC byte $FF"},
        "7959": {"comment":"C = command"},
        "7960": {"comment":"Select card 0"},
        "7964": {"comment":"or card 1"},
        "7966": {"synopsis":"Card selected: the command's 6 bytes.","comment":"Chip select"},
        "7968": {"comment":"Clock one byte first"},
        "7970": {"comment":"Command"},
        "7975": {"comment":"Argument, high byte first"},
        "7987": {"comment":"CRC"},
        "7990": {"comment":"A = response"},
        "7993": {"comment":"0: accepted?"},
        "7995": {"comment":"Success"},
        "7997": {"synopsis":"Reads port $EB until a byte other than $FF, 50 x 256 times at most.\nExit: A = the byte ($FF on time-out).","comment":"50 x 256 tries"},
        "8000": {"synopsis":"One try."},
        "8002": {"comment":"Still $FF?"},
        "8011": {"synopsis":"Waits for the data token $FE, up to 10 times SD_WAIT_BYTE.\nExit: Z the token; NZ not (Fc=1 for a byte below $FE).","comment":"10 tries"},
        "8013": {"synopsis":"One try."},
        "8016": {"comment":"Data token?"},
        "8040": {"synopsis":"The data.","comment":"HL = buffer"},
        "8043": {"comment":"B = 0: 256 bytes a time"},
        "8046": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "8050": {"comment":"CRC bytes passed over"},
        "8056": {"comment":"Success"},
        "8057": {"synopsis":"Ends a card operation, AF kept: a byte clocked, the card deselected (port $E7 = $FF),\nanother byte clocked.","comment":"Keep the result"},
        "8058": {"comment":"Clock a byte"},
        "8060": {"comment":"Deselect"},
        "8065": {"comment":"Clock a byte"},
        "8069": {"synopsis":"Sends command $4C (CMD12, stop transmission) with argument 0 to card Z (0) / NZ (1), then\nSD_DESELECT.","comment":"CMD12: stop transmission"},
        "8082": {"synopsis":"Writes the 512 bytes at IX to address HLDE of card Z (0) / NZ (1): command $58 (CMD24, one\nblock), token $FE, the data through two OTIRs, $FF twice for the CRC; the data response must\nbe 5 (accepted); the busy time waited out; then command $4D (CMD13) reads the status, whose\nsecond byte must be 0.\nExit: Fc=1; Fc=0 A = 0 (rc_ready: command or response failed), 1 (rc_wp: status bit 0, 1 or\n5), 3 (rc_crc: other status bits). Ends through SD_DESELECT.","comment":"Keep the card choice"},
        "8083": {"comment":"CMD24: write one block"},
        "8088": {"comment":"Refused?"},
        "8090": {"comment":"Data token"},
        "8094": {"comment":"Port $EB"},
        "8097": {"comment":"HL = data"},
        "8100": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "8104": {"comment":"CRC bytes"},
        "8112": {"comment":"Data response"},
        "8115": {"comment":"Accepted (5)?"},
        "8121": {"synopsis":"Card busy while it reads 0.","comment":"Still busy?"},
        "8127": {"comment":"Card choice back"},
        "8128": {"comment":"CMD13: status"},
        "8135": {"comment":"Refused?"},
        "8137": {"comment":"Status, second byte"},
        "8139": {"comment":"0: all well"},
        "8143": {"comment":"Bit 0, 1 or 5?"},
        "8145": {"comment":"rc_wp"},
        "8149": {"comment":"rc_crc"},
        "8153": {"synopsis":"Failure before the status.","comment":"Drop the card choice"},
        "8154": {"synopsis":"Error 0 (rc_ready).","comment":"rc_ready"},
        "8159": {"synopsis":"Adds 1 to the 32-bit counter at IX + $2B (the volume's free-cluster count in range B's\nnotes).","comment":"Low byte"},
        "8175": {"synopsis":"A = IX + $21, the volume's sectors per cluster."},
        "8179": {"synopsis":"Sets CONMEM (port $E3 = $80, RAM bank 0), then returns through the automap-off area: the\nfetch at $1FF8 ends the automap while CONMEM keeps this ROM paged for the RET. AF kept. From\n$03EB and the RST $08 handler ($0549).","comment":"Keep AF"},
        "8180": {"comment":"CONMEM on, bank 0"},
        "8184": {"comment":"Fetch here ends the automap"},
        "8185": {"synopsis":"RET in the automap-off area ($1FF8-$1FFF): jumped to (from $0042, $0076, $0404, $045A,\nDIVMMC_RELEASE), it returns with the automapped DivMMC memory released after this fetch,\nwhen NextReg $BB bit 6 enables the area.","comment":"Return, automap off"},
        "8186": {"comment":"No reference from this ROM"},
        "8188": {"synopsis":"Interrupt exit from $00EB: HL and AF back, interrupts on, return; the fetch at $1FFC ends\nthe automap.","comment":"HL back"},
        "8189": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "8190": {"comment":"Interrupts on"}
      }
    }
  },
